# What never belongs in a deployment upload.
#
# Without this the CLI uploaded 590MB, nearly all of it .local: the embedded Postgres data
# directory and the local blob store. That is development data from one machine. It has no business
# leaving it, and it makes every deploy slow for no reason.
#
# Deliberately conservative. `scripts` and `test` stay, because the build runs
# scripts/check-bundle.mjs and tsc reads the whole project. Excluding them saves a few hundred
# kilobytes and breaks the build, which is a bad trade.

.local
.env.local
.env.production.local
vercel-env.txt

# Build output. Vercel runs the build itself; a stale local copy only invites confusion.
dist

# The committed example site and its full-resolution source photos: reference material, not runtime.
sample
